],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"If this creature gets enough -1/-1 counters put on it to cause its toughness to be 0 or less (or the damage marked on it to be lethal), modular will put a number of +1/+1 counters on the target artifact creature equal to the number of +1/+1 counters on this creature before it left the battlefield.","oracle_id":"6d9af084-cd5d-4242-b0f0-24a36d0a75d4","published_at":"2006-09-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Each additional Hardened Scales you control will increase the number of +1/+1 counters placed on a creature you control by one.","oracle_id":"a1f3da21-af6d-450e-bf0b-985d158418e6","published_at":"2023-09-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a creature you control would enter the battlefield with a number of +1/+1 counters on it, it enters with that many plus one instead.","oracle_id":"a1f3da21-af6d-450e-bf0b-985d158418e6","published_at":"2023-09-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If two or more effects attempt to modify how many counters would be put on a creature you control, you choose the order to apply those effects, no matter who controls the sources of those effects.","oracle_id":"a1f3da21-af6d-450e-bf0b-985d158418e6","published_at":"2023-09-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a creature you control would enter the battlefield with a number of +1/+1 counters on it, it enters with twice that many instead.","oracle_id":"ca0cc02b-b106-4eca-9388-d4b48dd3be49","published_at":"2017-11-17","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you control two Corpsejack Menaces, the number of +1/+1 counters put on a creature is four times the original number. Three Corpsejack Menaces multiplies the original number by eight, and so on.","oracle_id":"ca0cc02b-b106-4eca-9388-d4b48dd3be49","published_at":"2017-11-17","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Wren's Run Packmaster gives deathtouch to all Wolf permanents you control, not just the tokens it creates.","oracle_id":"d4d27fef-e86b-4dd3-a15e-a0db8d0725ee","published_at":"2007-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A Wolf's deathtouch ability will apply if both Wren's Run Packmaster and that Wolf are on the battlefield at the time the Wolf deals damage. The creature dealt damage by the Wolf will be destroyed the next time state-based actions are checked, even if the Wolf or Wren's Run Packmaster leaves the battlefield.","oracle_id":"d4d27fef-e86b-4dd3-a15e-a0db8d0725ee","published_at":"2009-10-01","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
